The Rust code had [38;5;10mif !initialized || pattern.is_empty() { return; }[0m. The C code checks [38;5;10mif (!initialized || !pattern)[0m — which only guards against a NULL pointer, not an empty string. An empty [38;5;10m""[0m in C is a valid non-NULL pointer, so [38;5;10mfind_patterns("")[0m proceeds normally (and [38;5;10mstrstr(token.value, "")[0m always matches, per C semantics).[0m[0m
